Two, and both are overrides on `:root` or `body` in the core stylesheet rather than defaults you set [1].

**`--dp-z`.** Below the sheet breakpoint VitePress raises its own sidebar to 60 and its backdrop to 50, so a "modal" sheet left at 29 would render underneath the hamburger menu. The core raises it inside a media query [1]:

```css
@media (max-width: 959px) {
  :root { --dp-z: 70; }
}
```

**`--dp-fab-clear`.** With no floating button on the page — `ui.trigger: ['nav']` with `panel: 'popup'` is an ordinary configuration — the popup reserves no room under itself. It is written as the **absence** of the button so a browser without `:has()` keeps the room, which is the miss in the safe direction [1]:

```css
body:not(:has(.docpilot-nav-trigger.is-fab)) {
  --dp-fab-clear: 0px;
}
```

Everything else in the set of 34 you override yourself, loaded after the package's CSS [2][3][4]. Nine tokens differ in the dark set, and `--dp-wash` and `--dp-lip` are absent from it on purpose because both are derived from `--dp-text` [5].

